course: dictionary
lesson: 3617
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 3
explain: «Fils» is a French word. It means son, and it sounds like «feess». You will not find it in an English dictionary as an everyday word, but you may meet it in French lessons or in names.
explain: Context helps you see which meaning is right. «Dumas fils» is a name, and the word fils after it tells you this is the son, with the same name as his father. «Père et fils» means father and son. Ask: who is being talked about, and what would fit here?
explain: Money is a third meaning. «1000 fils = 1 Kuwaiti dinar» in a maths problem tells you a fils is a small coin. It is a fraction of the dinar, or of the dirham in the UAE. The numbers around the word show you that it is about money.
fact: «Fils» is French for son, and it sounds like «feess».
fact: «Mon fils» means my son in French.
fact: In English, «Dumas fils» means Dumas the son, to tell him apart from his father, who has the same name.
fact: A fils is a small coin, a fraction of the dinar or dirham, in some Arab countries like Kuwait, Bahrain and the UAE.
fact: 1000 fils = 1 Kuwaiti dinar, and 100 fils = 1 UAE dirham.
exercise: «Many family words come in a boy form and a girl form: un cousin and une cousine, un oncle and une tante, un fils and une fille.» In this sentence, what does fils mean? | Cousin | *Son | Coin | Daughter
exercise: In a maths problem, «1000 fils = 1 Kuwaiti dinar». What is a fils here? | A type of bread | *A small coin, a fraction of a dinar | A large coin worth ten dinars | A French word for daughter
exercise: In the name «Dumas fils», what does fils suggest? | The daughter of Dumas | The first Dumas in history | A town in France | *The son, with the same name as his father
test: In French, «mon fils» means? | my uncle | *my son | my daughter | my cousin
test: How many fils make 1 UAE dirham? | 1000 | *100 | 50 | 10
exam: In «père et fils», what does fils mean? | cousin | *son | father | coin
